{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-006/run/workspace","projectId":"91d2db77-2300-4ae4-961a-fea9e69f5ecf","parentId":"85625be3-b07d-4062-98d4-5be46dcea9d9","name":"Log sensitivity review and retention policy","details":"Inspect a representative sample of application logs for leaked secrets (auth tokens, session IDs, API keys, passwords), PII in URLs/query strings/error messages, and free-text fields that could contain either.

Define redaction patterns (regex and structured field rules), decide the retention window for raw vs. aggregated log data, and confirm the legal/security sign-off path.

Deliverable: redaction rule list + retention policy; the rule list becomes the direct input to the ingest-time redaction task in M2.","priority":10,"complexity":3,"estimatedHours":3,"tags":["governance","security","blocking-gate"]}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-006/run/workspace","projectId":"91d2db77-2300-4ae4-961a-fea9e69f5ecf","parentId":"85625be3-b07d-4062-98d4-5be46dcea9d9","name":"Agree non-functional targets: freshness, latency, volume","details":"Set concrete, testable numbers used later by the modeling and performance work: data freshness SLA (e.g. customer data by 07:00 daily, logs within 5 minutes), dashboard query p95 latency budget, concurrent user count, expected daily row and event volume, and the backfill horizon.

Also record the availability expectation and the acceptable data-staleness indicator behavior in the UI.

Deliverable: short NFR section appended to the requirements doc; each number must be measurable so M7 can test against it.","priority":8,"complexity":2,"estimatedHours":2,"tags":["requirements","nfr"]}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-006/run/workspace","projectId":"91d2db77-2300-4ae4-961a-fea9e69f5ecf","parentId":"d3bf3c47-478d-4a7e-9aa8-95402f5a7f8d","name":"Build CSV ingestion connector with incremental discovery","details":"Implement a loader that discovers new CSV drops in the landing zone, tracks processed files in a manifest (filename + checksum + load timestamp), and skips already-loaded files so reruns are idempotent.

Handle: encoding detection (UTF-8 vs Latin-1), delimiter/quote detection, header-to-column mapping, explicit type casting with null-safe parsing, and per-file load metadata (source file, row count, load time).

Scope limit: this task lands data into the raw table only - no business transformations. Deliverable: connector module plus a test covering a fresh load, a duplicate load, and a malformed-encoding file.","priority":9,"complexity":4,"estimatedHours":6,"tags":["ingestion","csv"]}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-006/run/workspace","projectId":"91d2db77-2300-4ae4-961a-fea9e69f5ecf","parentId":"d3bf3c47-478d-4a7e-9aa8-95402f5a7f8d","name":"Add CSV schema validation and row quarantine","details":"Define an expected-schema contract (column names, required vs optional, types, value ranges, allowed enums) and validate every file against it before load.

Two failure paths: file-level rejects (missing required column, unparseable header) stop the file and alert; row-level rejects go to a quarantine table with the raw row, reason code, and source file reference. Never silently drop a row.

Deliverable: validation module, quarantine table, and unit tests covering each reason code.","priority":9,"complexity":4,"estimatedHours":5,"tags":["ingestion","validation","data-quality"]}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-006/run/workspace","projectId":"91d2db77-2300-4ae4-961a-fea9e69f5ecf","parentId":"d3bf3c47-478d-4a7e-9aa8-95402f5a7f8d","name":"Parse and normalize log lines into structured events","details":"Write parsers for each log format in scope (assume a mix of JSON lines and plain-text patterns) and normalize into one event schema: timestamp (UTC), service, level, status code, latency, error signature, message, trace id.

